From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 16:14:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 6, second batch: Win-Back bounce/complaint-rate
 auto-pause with delivery monitoring for 6 of 7 email platforms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The last remaining Phase 6 item: "adds bounce/complaint monitoring with
auto-pause for Win-Back's send tolerance." User's explicit instruction:
build coverage for all 7 platforms Win-Back can send through, not a
prioritized subset — this batch does that, with an honest accounting of
what each platform's real API actually supports rather than fabricated
parity across all 7.

RESEARCH FIRST: a background agent attempted to verify each platform's
real bounce/complaint webhook mechanics against official docs. WebFetch
was entirely blocked in this sandbox (confirmed against unrelated
control domains) — every finding below is WebSearch-derived, not
WebFetch-confirmed, and flagged as such in each route's own header
comment. This surfaced two findings that changed the architecture for 3
of 7 platforms before any code was written:
  - HubSpot has no webhook for marketing-email bounce/complaint (its
    Webhooks API is CRM-object-change-based only) — poll-only via a
    legacy Email Events API instead.
  - GHL's bounce/complaint data (LC Email marketplace webhooks) requires
    a registered GHL Marketplace OAuth app + lc-email.readonly scope —
    a materially different, larger integration than this codebase's
    existing per-location API-key model, comparable in scope to standing
    up an entire new OAuth provider. Not built; documented as a real,
    scoped gap instead of silently faked.
  - Raw SMTP has no vendor/webhook concept at all — bounce detection
    reuses the existing per-engagement inbound-reply forwarding bridge
    plus a new classifier adapted from reply-classifier.ts's own
    already-proven bounce-language regex.

SHARED ARCHITECTURE (new):
- espDeliveryEvents table (schema.ts, migration 0054) — normalized
  bounce/complaint event log, idempotency via the existing webhookEvents
  table (same convention every other webhook route already follows).
- esp-delivery-events.ts — recordDeliveryEvent + getRollingDeliveryStats
  (7-day rolling window, enrollment count as the sends denominator —
  documented as a real approximation, not a precision claim: the true
  per-touch send count for the 6 ESP-driven cadences isn't visible to
  this app at all).
- esp-delivery-monitor.ts — checkAndApplyAutoPause (threshold check,
  sample-size floor, bulk-exits every active enrollment via the
  EXISTING exitWinBackSequence machinery already used for manual stops
  and rebook-exits, sets a stack-level pause flag, alerts the operator)
  and resumeWinBackSends (operator-initiated, does not fake
  re-enrollment). EngagementStack gains
  win_back_bounce_rate_threshold/complaint_rate_threshold/
  delivery_sample_minimum/auto_paused(+_at/_reason) — all jsonb, no
  migration needed.
- worker-blocking-conditions.ts — new "win-back-bounce-complaint-pause"
  condition, wired into BOTH enrollment call sites (the real
  cancellation-webhook path in pile-on/server/enrollment-service.ts,
  and the manual chat-winback.ts path) — gated before the atomic-claim
  insert so a paused engagement creates no enrollment row at all,
  correctly stopping the SMS/SMTP legs too (they key off the same row),
  matching "pause the whole cadence" literally rather than email-only.
- exitWinBackSequence gains a 4th reason ("auto_paused"), with
  ActiveCampaign's and Mailchimp's markRebooked fixed to NOT collapse it
  into a "rebooked" tag (a real correctness bug this would otherwise
  have introduced — an auto-paused contact would show as "rebooked" in
  the buyer's own CRM).
- resume-sends API route + a UI banner/control in
  win-back-config-form.tsx (pause reason, timestamp, resume button) plus
  per-platform webhook-URL/secret configuration UI, and an honest amber
  notice when email_platform is "ghl" ("not monitored," never a
  false-looking "0%").

PER-PLATFORM INGESTION (new webhook routes under
src/app/api/webhooks/*-delivery/[engagementId]/, each with its own
verification-status header comment):
- klaviyo-delivery — HMAC-SHA256(body+timestamp)/Klaviyo-Signature,
  MEDIUM confidence; bounce topic reasonably corroborated, spam-complaint
  topic UNVERIFIED (may need a paid add-on) — matched defensively on
  topic substrings, not one hardcoded guessed string.
- mailchimp-delivery — Marketing API's real (weaker) model: NO
  cryptographic signature, a ?secret= query param + a required GET
  reachability handshake. Bounce and complaint both arrive as
  type=cleaned, distinguished by data[reason] "hard" vs "abuse" — the
  single most load-bearing unverified fact in this route, logged loudly
  when it doesn't match either.
- activecampaign-delivery — bounce is real and detected; complaint is
  NOT built (no confirmed distinct event type exists, evidence suggests
  it folds into ordinary unsubscribe with no confirmed field to
  distinguish spam from an ordinary opt-out) — an honest gap, not a
  guessed proxy. Signature header NAME is the operator's own choice in
  AC's UI (new stack field), secret in the vault.
- convertkit-delivery — this app's ConvertKitClient confirmed (from its
  own code) to use API v3, not v4; v3 has no confirmed signature scheme
  at all, so none is claimed — the engagement-scoped URL itself is the
  access control, same posture already established for the
  inbound-reply bridge. Bounce/complaint matched defensively on payload
  substrings.
- SMTP — no route; extends the existing inbound-reply forwarding bridge
  with a bounce classifier (smtp-bounce-classifier.ts) reusing
  reply-classifier.ts's own proven delivery-failure phrasing, narrowed
  to exclude OOO/vacation matches. Complaint detection for raw SMTP is
  NOT buildable (no client-side signal exists — FBL registration is a
  separate, bilateral, per-mailbox-provider undertaking) — documented,
  not silently dropped.
- HubSpot — no webhook exists to build against; a real poll fan-out
  instead (hubspot-delivery-poll-cron, every 15 min, HubSpotClient
  .pollDeliveryEvents against the legacy Email Events API, a per-
  engagement watermark that only advances on a successful poll).
- GHL — deliberately not built; documented gap (see above).

TESTS (new, real automated coverage, not just code review):
- smtp-bounce-classifier.test.ts — 11 cases, pure regex logic (bounce
  vs. genuine reply vs. OOO, recipient extraction).
- esp-delivery-monitor.test.ts — 9 cases covering
  checkAndApplyAutoPause's real orchestration logic (already-paused
  no-op, sample floor, threshold crossing on either metric, bulk exit
  fan-out count and arguments, SMTP's no-ESP-call path, a client
  threshold override) and resumeWinBackSends (clears exactly the 3 pause
  keys, leaves the rest of the stack untouched) — collaborators
  (getRollingDeliveryStats, exitWinBackSequence, resolveCredential,
  notifyUser) mocked out so these tests verify this module's own control
  flow, not re-verify its collaborators' internals.

Verification: npx tsc --noEmit stayed at the established baseline of 5
pre-existing errors in unrelated test files. `next build`'s compile and
TypeScript phases both pass cleanly; its page-data collection step still
fails in this sandbox on DATABASE_URL not being set, the same
pre-existing sandbox limitation confirmed throughout this session. npx
vitest run: 59 failed / 210 passed / 18 skipped — the established
baseline (59/191/18) plus exactly the 19 new tests in this commit, none
of them among the 59 pre-existing failures.

